Blocky is a fast and lightweight DNS proxy and ad-blocker for local
networks, written in Go. It blocks queries against configurable deny
and allow lists (per client group), forwards to one or more upstream
resolvers with selectable strategies, supports conditional forwarding,
custom DNS mappings, response caching with prefetching and optional
Prometheus metrics.

Note: Blocky answers on the DNS port (53 by default). When running it
on port 53 you must either disable the built-in Unbound/Dnsmasq
resolver or run Blocky on an alternate port and forward to it.

WWW: https://0xerr0r.github.io/blocky/
